WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.737
OK.

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.138
Gonna check this trap here.

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:11.177
I see something moving in there.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:13.113
What the hell's that?

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.948
Something's growling.

00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:17.283
It's like this deep moo.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.284
OK.

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:24.791
[screaming]

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:34.134
There's something in there.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.837
I have a feeling I know
exactly what it is.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.410
[grunting]

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:45.412
I think there's an
electric eel in there.

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:49.749
Right there.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:52.385
You see that?

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:55.422
I got a slithering eel in there.

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:58.558
Electric eels can
produce a shocking jolt

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:00.894
of over 650 volts.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.830
[screaming]

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:06.299
Aye, aye, aye.

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:08.368
It's just like
sticking your finger

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:11.171
right into a light socket.

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:15.909
It's an adaptation the
eels have for hunting prey,

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:20.180
navigating in murky
water, and self-defense.

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:24.417
OK, get out of there.

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:25.752
Look at that.

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:28.721
That is an electric eel.

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:30.857
Do you hear that?

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.025
That's crazy.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:37.330
OK, come on.

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:39.899
Go back in the water.

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.100
Go back in the water.

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:52.512
They're very mysterious, very
ugly, but amazing animal.

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:55.415
Their whole bodies
are just full of fat,

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:57.150
like hardly any muscle at all.

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:59.919
And, yeah, as far
as eating them goes,

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:04.624
there are very few
tribes that eat them.

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:05.959
I have tried 'em myself.

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:10.096
They're just, like,
lard, goo, gelatin.

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:13.199
Yeah, it's not nice, not nice.

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:17.837
Thankfully, the eel isn't the
only fish caught in the trap.

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:21.374
The catfish is alive, but
it can't move because it's

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:24.110
been stunned by that eel.

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:27.280
Basically they were
trapped together.

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:29.182
Oh, man.

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:31.451
Big meaty fish.

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:34.587
[music playing]

